extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 101-102 (cache p102-p103; text layer, page_offset +1): the Wing Blade, read against renders; source_book cites the body''s own pages. The shared skills, issue and money are the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.''s, printed 97-98 (cache p098-p099). The chapter rules on printed 96 and 98-99 were read too. Printed 100 (cache p101) is a full-page illustration with no text. || SHARED SKILLS: the five Republic cyborg classes (republic-cyborg-soldier, dragon-borg-wing-blade, dragon-borg-tsunami, dragon-borg-imperial-combat, dragon-borg-flame-cloud) restate ONE skill list, the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.''s (printed 97-98), and MUST BE CHANGED TOGETHER. Printed 101 says the dragon ''borgs have the same O.C.C. skills as the cyborg soldier unless a police officer or mercenary. Identical in all five: O.C.C., related and secondary skills, hand to hand, XP table, starting money, occ_group and men_of_arms, the M.E. requirement, the human-only race restriction and the standard military issue. What differs is the body: the four dragon ''borgs are one class per body (mdc_base, fixed P.S./P.P./Spd, unconditional combat bonuses, weapons and features), following the Free Quebec cyborgs (fq-cyborg-*, BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F31). || XP: the Dragon Borg, Japanese Borg column on the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, printed folio 216), fourth column, bottom block, read off a render: 0 / 2,176 / 4,301 / 8,401 / 17,501 / 24,601 / 36,701 / 44,801 / 57,901 / 94,001 / 130,001 / 190,001 / 240,001 / 280,001 / 330,001. || GROUP: men-of-arms with men_of_arms: true in all five Republic cyborg classes, following fq-cyborg-soldier and cs-cyborg-strike-trooper; the book files the Republic''s cyborgs with no group heading. The soldier states no pool, so the line picks its S.D.C. roll; a dragon ''borg states mdc_base, and the line is kept so the five agree. || BODY AND BONUSES: the body''s fixed P.S. 24, P.P. 22 and Spd 176 (printed 101) are stored as attribute_dice, as for the other three dragon ''borgs and this book''s ninja-borg. The stat block''s unconditional combat bonuses (+2 attacks including tail, neck and arm bonuses, +2 initiative, +2 parry, +1 dodge, +2 pull punch, +1 roll, +2 vs horror factor) are stored; the P.P. 22 bonus of +4 to strike, parry and dodge the book prints is what the sheet derives from the stored P.P. and is not added again. The wings'' +10% to jet pack piloting (feature 18), and -20% with a wing lost, are the body''s and are prose in the Folding Wings ability, not folded into the shared Jet Packs figure. || M.D.C.: mdc_base is the main body only (270). By location: hands 15 each, arms (4) 40 each, legs 110 each, tail 50 per 6 ft length, cheek blades 10 each, wings 90 each, head 90, neck 120, neck and knee cameras 2 each, nose horn 15, head horns 10 each, removable jet thruster 80, ten maneuvering thrusters 5 each. The body has no vehicles row; the chassis is in special_abilities, side_effects and the body. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Radio: Basic 45+10, Computer Operation 40+10, Jet Packs 42+20 (printed Pilot Jet Pack), Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10, Find Contraband 26+10 (printed Find Contraband, Weapons & Cybernetics), Land Navigation 36+10, Climbing 40+10, Swimming 50+10. Literacy: Japanese at 98% stored as Literacy: Native Language at the book''s 98, fixed; Language: Japanese 98% as Language: Native Tongue; one language of choice (+15%) as a Language: Other pick. W.P. Heavy Energy Weapons is W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons, as fq-cyborg-soldier stores it. Hand to Hand: Basic Martial Arts/Judo is this book''s row; the upgrade prices (Aikido or Karate one pick, Jujitsu two) are the hand_to_hand block. The Jet Packs figure is the soldier''s +20% in all five; a body''s own bonus to jet pack piloting stays in that body''s prose. || RELATED: five plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. SECONDARY: none at level one; two each at levels 2, 5, 8 and 13, as printed (the FQ soldier''s ninth-level slot is 8 here), from the related list excluding those marked None and without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the standard military issue (printed 98), identical in all five Republic cyborg classes: the energy rifle is unspecified, so it is a choice of this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand energy rifles (the stun rifle and the underwater rifle left out); four extra E-clips are the rifle E-clip row; four grenades are a choice of this book''s grenades excluding the armor dissolver, as printed (four of one kind; a mix is the GM''s call); distancing binoculars are infrared-distancing-binoculars; the backpack is pr-1-standard-backpack, this book''s standard pack. The body-styling ammunition, maintenance and repairs are not items, and the jet pack, hover vehicle and extra weapons available upon assignment are not starting kit. The Wing Blade adds its leg-compartment contents. The book prints the compartments twice, as one in each leg (feature 7) and as two in each leg (weapon system 6); one set of contents is stored. The laser rod has no catalog row and is not offered. || MONEY: monthly salary 2,000 credits (officers of 9th level and up 3,500 to 5,000; police ''borgs 800 more than an unaugmented officer); starting_money holds the 1D6x1000 the book gives as a first-level character''s savings. Room, board, clothing and medical care are provided. The text layer ciphers the savings as !D6xlOOO."
