## Lore

Across much of Japan full conversion cyborgs are thought of as freaks or
monsters, but among the Cyberoids of the Republic they are ordinary, respected
and often admired. That comfort with bionics is what made the dragon ''borgs
possible. Dragons stand for strength, wisdom and magic, and the people who
become dragon ''borgs take on the same symbolism; nobody recalls whose idea the
inhuman styling was, but it has proved wildly popular. ArmaTech builds them
only for the Republic''s military and police.

The AT-C8000 Wing Blade takes its name from its bat-like mechanical wings and
its long prehensile tail lined with blades, but it is better known as the
"Snoop." It is a spy and reconnaissance body. Its long flexible neck lets it
look over walls and around corners, high or low, without showing itself, and
push its head into small openings and air ducts. Its legs are made for leaping
and a loping run, to get in and out quickly and dodge attacks, and its tail
can snake around corners to snatch an item, probe small spaces, or strike and
entangle a foe. It is silent, carries cameras and sound recorders, has four
arms and a slender body, and folds its wings so that it can fly and still fit
almost anywhere.

## The chassis

The standard AT-C8000 Wing Blade, a full conversion cyborg for espionage and
light assault. Weapons and bionic features may differ slightly from one ''borg
to the next.

- Height: about five feet (1.5 m) for the body; seven feet (2.1 m) with the
  wings folded and the head held low, five feet crouched. Extended wings add
  12 feet (3.6 m).
- Width: 2 1/2 feet (0.75 m) for the body, 3 1/2 feet (1 m) with wings folded.
- Length: 23 feet in all, with a six-foot (1.8 m) neck and a 12-foot (3.6 m)
  tail.
- Weight: 1000 lbs (450 kg).
- Physical attributes: equal to P.S. 24, P.P. 22, Spd 176.
- Running 120 mph (192 km); leaping 25 feet (7.6 m) high or long, a running
  leap adding 1D4x10 yards/meters; flight by jet pack only.
- Power: nuclear, average life 20 years.
- Market cost: six million credits with all standard features and weapons.
  Poor availability; outside the Republic only Ichto makes them, at 10% more.

## GM Notes

A Wing Blade pilot is a Republic cyborg soldier (or police officer, or
mercenary) in a dragon body. Standard military issue covers all ammunition and
equipment for the body''s weapon systems, and a jet pack, hover vehicle,
further weapons and equipment are available upon assignment, depending on the
local commander, supply, location, casualties and combat conditions. The
character has medium security clearance to most military bases, hospitals and
facilities, and standard military rank, private to general. Soldiers live in
dormitory-style barracks, four to an area, or off base at their own expense.

On leaving service a ''borg may keep basic bionics as a registered citizen,
keep most systems after a long or heroic career if authorized, or be
retro-fitted with bio-systems or moved into a clone body (printed 98). The
Republic''s laws on cybernetics are harsh (printed 99).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-wing-blade');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-wing-blade';

